DNS(Domain Name System)
TTL(Time To Live)
ISP(Internet Server Provider)
TLD(Top Level Domain: .com, .org, .net...)
ccTLD(Country Code Top Level Domain: .uk, .us .su...)

Key DNS Record Types:

Record | Purpose                           | Example
###########################################################################
A      | Domain -> IPv4                    | google.com -> 142.250.185.46
AAAA   | Domain -> IPv6                    | google.com -> 2607:f8b0::...
CNAME  | Alias -> another domain           | www -> google.com
MX     | Mail server for domain            | google.com -> smtp.google.com
NS     | Authoritative maneservers         | google.com -> ns1.google.com
TXT    | Arbirtary text(SPF, verification) | "v=spf1 include:..."

The 4 Actors:

Browser
|
Recursive Resolver # ISP's(Internet Server Provider) or a public one
|
Root Nameserver    # Knows where TLD(Top Level Domain) servers are
|
TLD Nameserver     # Knows who owns .com, .org, .net etc.
| Authoritative NS   # Knows the actual IP for google.com
